.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception
.Dd October 30, 2026
.Dt NQKSTMT 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqkstmt
.Nd make a key statement: a rotation or a revocation
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fo nqkstmt
.Fa "nqsalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *pk" "size_t pklen"
.Fa "nqsalg nalg" "const uint8_t *nsk" "size_t nsklen"
.Fa "const uint8_t *npk" "size_t npklen"
.Fa "int64_t at" "const char *reason"
.Fa "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Fc
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn nqkstmt
writes to
.Fa out ,
of
.Fa cap
bytes, a key statement
.Pq Ql noqtis-keys-1 , Xr noqtis-capsule 5
in canonical JSON.
With
.Fa nsk
and
.Fa npk
given, it is a rotation: the holder of the key pair
.Fa sk , pk
of
.Fa alg
says that from time
.Fa at
(seconds since 1970-01-01T00:00:00Z) it is replaced by
.Fa nsk , npk
of
.Fa nalg ,
and both keys sign it.
With
.Fa nsk
and
.Fa npk
.Dv NULL ,
it is a revocation of
.Fa pk
from
.Fa at ,
signed by it.
.Fa reason
is
.Dv NULL
or up to 255 bytes of UTF-8 with no control character.
.Fa *outlen
gets the statement's size, also when
.Fa cap
is too small.
.Pp
Each signature is verified before the statement is written.
.Xr nqchkx 3
follows statements from a trusted key through its
.Fa stmt
option.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Bl -tag -width NQENOSUP
.It Dv NQOK
The statement was written.
.It Bq Er NQEBUF
.Fa cap
is too small.
.It Bq Er NQENOSUP
An algorithm is not a post-quantum signature (Ed25519 alone).
.It Bq Er NQEARG
A
.Dv NULL
argument, keys of the wrong sizes or not a pair, the new key equal to
the old one,
.Fa at
before 1970 or after 9999, or a reason that is too long or not plain
text.
.It Bq Er NQEMEM
The allocation hook returned
.Dv NULL .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-revoke 1 ,
.Xr noqtis-rotate 1 ,
.Xr nqchkx 3 ,
.Xr noqtis-capsule 5
